  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The space–time diagram shows coordinate axes of inertial reference frames S(x, ct) and S′(x′, ct′). Event X occurs at t = 1 s according to the S reference frame. A line of constant space–time interval is drawn through X.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>In the S′ reference frame, which event is simultaneous with X and which event has the time coordinate t′ = 1 s?</p>\n<p><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
  },
